Whee, my first Lojban translations!

la lojban be skami panru la glibau zo'e

The zo'e is intended stylistically, to help match the feel of
'essentially'.  There appears to be no word for 'calculus' in lojban,
which surprised me until I thought about it.  :-)

la lojban be le esperantos. bangu prenu be'o panru la cmaci bridi zo'e

I wasn't sure about whether the be'o needs to be there, so I went for
safety.  Also, it may be stylistically nicer to use selbanka'e instead
of bangu, but I went for shorter instead.

What _is_ the standard word for Esperanto?  I thought I had seen it
somewhere.

